wikipedia_extract: 'Sakawa (酒匂) was the last of four Agano-class light cruisers built
  for the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) during World War II. Fuel shortages crippled
  the IJN''s operations by the time the ship was completed in late 1944 and she never
  left Japanese waters. After the war, Sakawa was used to ferry Japanese troops home
  until she was selected in early 1946 to be expended for nuclear weapon tests during
  Operation Crossroads. The ship was used as a target during the first bomb test on
  1 July and sank the following day.


